      "writtenOn": "2023-08-08T08:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I wrote the only thing that should take long time (about 250ms) and should only be called one time during boot is NCL_DRBG-\u003einit() , and unfortunately this cannot work in non-blocking mode. If you do not want the reseed (the generation of a new 128 byte random seed) to happen , every 100 calls to NCL_DRBG-\u003egenerate(), you can change the ‘100’ in the config function to a bigger number or even maxint like this: NCL_DRBG-\u003econfig(ctx_p, 0xFFFFFFFF, false)",
